{ Welcome to Chapter 1 of our White repertoire — mark this entry as Informational on Chessable.<br><br>Facing 1... d5 2. c4 e6, we choose the Classical Queen's Gambit Declined with 4. Bg5 and 5. e3 before Nf3. This disciplined move order gives us rich Karpov-style space and structural mastery while ruling out three huge theoretical headaches. } 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 { Even on move 3, Black can test our preparation with the Triangle Slav, Alatortsev, Tarrasch, or QGD Stonewall — click any sideline below to see our exact setup. } { [%csl Ye6,Rd5] [%cal Gc4d5] } ( 3... c6 4. e4 { — Triangle Slav: we strike with the Marshall Gambit 4. e4! and bypass Noteboom theory.<br><br>If Black avoids ...Nf6 with 3... Be7?: } ) ( 3... Be7 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bf4 { — Alatortsev order: immediate cxd5 and Bf4 keeps our options flexible.<br><br>Against the Tarrasch 3... c5?: } ) ( 3... c5 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. g3 { — Tarrasch Defense: Karpov's surgical fianchetto aimed directly at the isolated d5 pawn.<br><br>And against 3... f5?: } ) ( 3... f5 4. Bf4 c6 5. e3 { — Stonewall via QGD order: immediate Bf4 clamps e5 and gives White a commanding +1.23 edge. } ) 4. Bg5 { 4. Bg5 before Nf3 is our ironclad move-order anchor.<br><br>Developing Nf3 prematurely lets Black drag us into the Vienna Variation, the Classical Ragozin, or the Botvinnik complex — 4. Bg5 keeps all three locked out. } { [%csl Yg5] [%cal Bg5f6] } ( 4. Nf3 $6 Bb4 { — Prohibited move order: 4. Nf3?! allows the Classical Ragozin, Vienna 4... dxc4, and Botvinnik complexes. } ) 4... Be7 { 4... Be7 enters the Classical Orthodox setup. Watch our mandatory move-order rule if Black tries 4... c6 instead: } ( 4... c6 5. e3 { — Mandatory Anti-Botvinnik guard: 5. e3! defends c4 with the f1 bishop and steers calmly back into Orthodox or Cambridge Springs. } ) 5. e3 { 5. e3! completes our shield before developing Nf3, keeping Botvinnik and Anti-Moscow doors shut. } { [%csl Ye3] [%cal Bf1d3,Bg5h4] } 5... O-O 6. Nf3 { With 6. Nf3 we enter the Classical QGD tabiya. Throughout Chapter 1 you will master four reusable structural blueprints:<br><br>• Carlsbad Structure — cxd5 exd5 with either the b2-b4-b5 Minority Attack or f2-f3 and e3-e4.<br><br>• Pressure on d5 — Tartakower 8. Qb3! and 11. Rd1!, targeting d5 and central files.<br><br>• Open c-File and Rook Lift — Lasker 9. Rc1! and 10. Rxc3! alongside Cambridge Springs, keeping our structure intact.<br><br>• Targeted Fianchettoes — Karpov's 6. g3 against the Tarrasch IQP and positional 5. g3! against the Albin. } { [%csl Gd4,Gc4] [%cal Bg5h4,Bf1d3,Ba1c1] } *

