{ Today's most popular grandmaster test after 13. Bb3: Black slams the center shut with 13... e4, hoping to suffocate our kingside before we strike back at the base. } 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Be7 5. e3 O-O 6. Nf3 Nbd7 7. Rc1 c6 8. Bd3 dxc4 9. Bxc4 Nd5 10. Bxe7 Qxe7 11. O-O Nxc3 12. Rxc3 e5 13. Bb3 e4 { 13... e4 is a major structural shift: the center locks, Black gains kingside space for ...Nf6 and ...f5, and White's f3 knight is kicked. Our agenda switches instantly from open e-file play to undermining e4 with f2-f3 and Qc2. } { [%csl Re4,Yd4] [%cal Re4f3] } 14. Nd2 $1 { 14. Nd2! is the only square that preserves our advantage. The knight immediately eyes e4 and c4 while clearing the f-pawn so f2-f3 can detonate the Black wedge.<br><br>Retreating 14. Ne1? looks safe on autopilot, yet drops all pressure and hands Black the initiative.<br><br>━━━ PLAN FROM HERE ━━━<br><br>Verdict: +0.25 to +0.30 — Locked Center with Immediate f2-f3 Counter-Break<br><br>• Our Plan — Prepare f2-f3 after h3 or Qc2, reroute Nd2 to c4 and Rc3 to c5, and use the b3 bishop to pressure f7 once the f-file opens.<br><br>• Watch Out — Black wants ...Nf6, ...Bf5 or ...Kh8 with ...f5 to cement e4; never let Black stabilize e4 unchallenged.<br><br>• Key Trades & Endgame — Exchange Black's light-squared bishop if it lands on e6 or f5, or trade off one pair of rooks after f3 exf3 so our queen and knight dominate e4 and c5.<br><br><br>━━━ SAMPLE CONTINUATIONS ━━━<br><br>See how White undermines e4 or squeezes the queenside depending on Black's 14th move: } { [%csl Re4,Yf3,Bc4] [%cal Gf2f3,Bd2c4,Bc3c5,Rd7f6] } ( 14. Ne1 $2 Nf6 15. f3 Bf5 { — Autopilot mistake — -0.20 to -0.31: passive knight gives Black time to cement e4 with ...Bf5. } ) ( 14. Nd2 Nf6 15. h3 g6 16. f3 exf3 17. Qxf3 { — 94% practical reply: recapturing 17. Qxf3 rather than 17. Rxf3 keeps the f1 rook ready to double and eyes f6 and f7 along the open f-file — +0.30.<br><br>If Black pushes on the queenside with 14... a5?: } ) ( 14. Nd2 a5 15. a4 Nf6 16. Rc5 { — Fixing a5 lets White's rook jump to c5 before playing Qc2 and f3 — +0.27. } ) *

